From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:12:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] installd: PlaitOS backup streams, review fixes

- zstd reader: drain output zstd still holds before reading more input,
  and treat the end of input inside a frame as a damaged archive.
- Restores need the end-of-archive blocks (a truncated tar is an error).
- Restores extract into <pkg>/.plait_restore and only replace the app's
  data once the whole archive arrived intact; a failed restore leaves
  the old data as it was. The app's dir (and its inode) stays.
- Backups open files with O_NONBLOCK and fstat the opened fd, so a file
  swapped for a FIFO can't hang installd.
- Directory depth limit (128) and one fd per level while walking.
- Restored directories keep setgid (never setuid).
- APK backups also from adopted storage (/mnt/expand/<uuid>/app).
- One copy buffer per stream; the extractor reuses the last parent dir.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
